      "side": 0,
      "message": "Correct me if I were wrong, so we should power off in time when all the below conditions are met:\n1) phone.SubId !\u003d dds (non-dds)\n2) data is disconnected (dcTracker.isDisconnected, of mPhone.subId)\n3) data of dds still connected.  (!ProxyController.getInstance().isDataDisconnected(dds))\n\nshouldn\u0027t that be:\nif (dcTracker.isDisconnected()\n    \u0026\u0026 (dds !\u003d mPhone.getSubId() \n        \u0026\u0026 !ProxyController.getInstance().isDataDisconnected(dds)\n       )\n    )?.\n\nAnd what about cases of dds \u003d\u003d mPhone.getSubId()? Even though it doesn\u0027t affect SS logic, then should it be:\n\nif (dcTracker.isDisconnected()\n    \u0026\u0026 !ProxyController.getInstance().isDataDisconnected(dds)\n    )?.\n\nIt\u0027s kind of confusing since there is only one condition here, i.e. just check dcTracker.isDisconn.",
